Here's the final `Program.cs`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase
};

var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new Person("Jane", 30), options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string Name, int Age);
```

Output: `{"name":"Jane","age":30}` ✅

The key is `JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` on `JsonSerializerOptions`. The record declaration goes after top-level statements (a C# requirement).
